B.Jp=s(["By default, each move has a 15-second clock \u2014 adjustable, or you can turn it off entirely before a game starts.","If time runs out, you simply lose that turn. Nothing moves and there's no extra penalty \u2014 but it applies even if you're in check, so if the clock is short, don't sit on a threatened Prime."],t.s)
B.Jt=s(["An Arc moves any distance along a curve \u2014 one ring and one wedge at a time. Because of how the checkering works, an Arc always stays on squares of one color, even as its path sweeps through the pole and out the far side of the board.","One of this Arc's diagonals runs all the way past the center to the far rim. The other meets a piece partway and stops there \u2014 with a capture."],t.s)
